From 8f22b2a916e4f825ab55ca9d364a44724b61ceb6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:06:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Trilinos: fast incomplete factorizations of ShyLU and block
 preconditioners of Teko

Fast incomplete factorizations (ShyLU FastILU): the types FAST_ILU,
FAST_ILU_B, FAST_IC and FAST_ILDL of the Ifpack2 entry, when Trilinos is
built with ShyLU_NodeFastILU, are applied to the diagonal block of each
process by the additive Schwarz method of Ifpack2 without overlap: Ifpack2
17.2.1 uses them as solvers of subdomains, and given a distributed matrix
they read the columns of the other processes as local rows (double free on
two processes); their parameters are checked when the preconditioner is
created, by a factorization of the chosen type. Without FastILU, these
types are refused with a hint.

Block preconditioners of Teko: new preconditioner Teko, when mfem-mgis
uses Teko (option enable-teko, AUTO by default: Trilinos built with Teko,
optional component of find_package, and double precision, the only type
Teko 17.2.1 is instantiated for). The unknowns of each node are split in
blocks of consecutive components (option Blocks, one block per component
by default; Teko::TpetraHelpers::StridedTpetraOperator). The option
Parameters defines the library of inverses of Teko (block Jacobi,
Gauss-Seidel... and the preconditioners and solvers of Stratimikos, MueLu
included), and Inverse selects the block preconditioner used: by default,
a block Jacobi preconditioner whose blocks are approximated by MueLu, or
the only block preconditioner of the definitions. The definitions are
checked when the preconditioner is created (types, names of the
definitions named after Stratimikos, indices and inverses referenced by
Inverse Type and Preconditioner Type, preconditioners given by Use
Preconditioner, inverse used being a block preconditioner), Teko 17.2.1
reporting these errors without explanation or crashing; the inverses of
type MueLu, the one of Stratimikos included, get the defaults of the
MueLu entry (silent, deterministic aggregation, factories not written
with Kokkos with several equations per node). Teko computes with the default
node of Tpetra; a process owning no unknown is refused by all the
processes (Teko fails on it while the others wait). Teko splits the
vectors in blocks on the host, with arrays of the global size of each
block: documented as a limitation.

Tests (TrilinosSolversTest, 1, 2 and 3 processes, CPU and GPU): FAST_ILU
and FAST_IC need close numbers of iterations to RILUK, the parameters of
FAST_ILU are given to the factorization and checked, block Jacobi with
MueLu for both orderings, block Gauss-Seidel with Amesos2 on blocks of two
and one components, default parameters, refusals of invalid definitions
and of an empty process; without Teko or FastILU, the refusals and their
hints.
